<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pemmican War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1812">1812</a>–<a href="/years/1821">1821</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pemmican War was a conflict between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River Colony</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manitoba">Manitoba</a>. It began when the colony's governor banned the export of pemmican, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> and fur traders' staple food, in 1814. The violence peaked at Seven Oaks in 1816, when twenty-one colonists were killed, and ended with the merger of the two companies in 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pemmican-war.jpg" alt="Pemmican War" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles William Jefferys · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Fight_at_Seven_Oaks.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
